That discussion mentions LCOC entries for Lojban:

"Searching "Lojban" at the Library of Congress Online Catalog returns
basically four records for works in Lojban: (1) *Lojbo karni* by the LLG,
(2) *Ju'i Lobypli* by R. LeChevalier, (3) *Hoi Loglypli* by R. LeChevalier,
(4) *Me la Uacintyn Loglytuan.* by R. LeChevalier."

Are all four of these entries in Lojban? It seems to me that only the first
two are. "logl-", "hoi", "tua(n)" smack of TLI Loglan.

stevo

